            "placeholder": "512m",
            "help": "Optional. The most memory this app's own container may use, for example 512m or 2g. A bare number means bytes to Docker, not megabytes. Left empty it gets 512m. Any database this app brings has its own separate ceiling."
        },
        {
            "name": "cpu_limit",
            "label": "CPU limit",
            "type": "text",
            "required": false,
            "advanced": false,
            "placeholder": "No limit",
            "help": "Optional. How many CPU cores this app's own container may use — 1 for one full core, 0.5 for half. This server has 4, and Docker will not start a container asking for more. Left empty there is no CPU limit at all. Going past this does not kill anything; the container waits, so the symptom is slowness rather than an error. Any database this app brings is not limited by it."
        }
